{"vid":"Oj0m9rvGk4w","source":"Oj0m9rvGk4w.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Well,"},{"t":1.5,"txt":"your sister stood me up the other night."},{"t":3.9,"txt":">> Oh, no. Don't you hate it when people"},{"t":6.3,"txt":"aren't there for you? [laughter]"},{"t":9.3,"txt":">> Well, did you try calling her?"},{"t":10.9,"txt":">> I've been trying for 2 days. When I"},{"t":12.9,"txt":"called the restaurant, they said she was"},{"t":14.3,"txt":"too busy to talk. I can't believe she's"},{"t":16.7,"txt":"blowing me off. [music]"},{"t":19.2,"txt":">> Think ignoring you is the same as"},{"t":21.2,"txt":"blowing you off? You're missing a huge"},{"t":24.2,"txt":"cultural cue that screams foreigner."},{"t":27.2,"txt":"Watch this."},{"t":29.5,"txt":">> [music]"},{"t":36.6,"txt":">> I'm on this field and they they hike"},{"t":38.6,"txt":"[snorts] me the baby"},{"t":41.2,"txt":"and I I know I've got to do something"},{"t":42.7,"txt":"cuz the Tampa Bay defense is coming"},{"t":44.5,"txt":"right at me."},{"t":46.3,"txt":">> Tampa Bay has got a terrible team,"},{"t":49.5,"txt":">> right? But"},{"t":52.1,"txt":"it is just me and the baby. So I'm"},{"t":54.1,"txt":"thinking they can take us."},{"t":61.2,"txt":">> I'm on this field and they they hike me"},{"t":63.8,"txt":"the baby. [laughter]"},{"t":65.7,"txt":">> Hike."},{"t":67.4,"txt":"Hike usually means a long walk in"},{"t":69.8,"txt":"nature. However, in American football,"},{"t":72.6,"txt":"it means to snap the ball to start a"},{"t":74.7,"txt":"play. Joey is using a sports metaphor"},{"t":77.7,"txt":"here. He isn't walking the baby. The"},{"t":80.3,"txt":"baby is being thrown to him to start the"},{"t":82.6,"txt":"game."},{"t":84.2,"txt":"The center hiked the ball and the"},{"t":86,"txt":"quarterback started running. It"},{"t":88.6,"txt":"describes the specific action of"},{"t":90.6,"txt":"starting a play in American football."},{"t":95.9,"txt":">> It is just me and the baby, so I'm"},{"t":98,"txt":"thinking they can take us."},{"t":101,"txt":">> Take us."},{"t":102.9,"txt":"Take us in this context is street slang"},{"t":105.4,"txt":"for defeat us or beat us in a fight."},{"t":108.5,"txt":"Joey thinks the opposing football team"},{"t":110.6,"txt":"can easily overpower him and the baby."},{"t":113.3,"txt":"It's a common way to assess your chances"},{"t":115.5,"txt":"in a competition or physical"},{"t":117.6,"txt":"confrontation."},{"t":119.9,"txt":"There are five of them and two of us. I"},{"t":122.2,"txt":"don't think we can take them. It"},{"t":124.8,"txt":"expresses doubt about winning a fight"},{"t":127,"txt":"against a larger group."},{"t":133.4,"txt":"What are you going to do?"},{"t":134.8,"txt":">> What can I do? Look, I don't want to do"},{"t":137,"txt":"anything to screw it up with Ursula and"},{"t":139,"txt":"your friend Phoebe. Well, if she's my"},{"t":141,"txt":"friend, hopefully she'll understand. I"},{"t":143,"txt":"mean, wouldn't you guys?"},{"t":144.6,"txt":">> Man, if you tried something like that on"},{"t":146.2,"txt":"my birthday, you'd be staring at the"},{"t":147.7,"txt":"business end of a hy fit."},{"t":152.8,"txt":">> What are you going to do?"},{"t":154.3,"txt":">> What can I do? Look, I don't want to do"},{"t":156.5,"txt":"anything to screw it up with Ursula and"},{"t":158.4,"txt":"your friend. Screw it up. Screw it up is"},{"t":161.7,"txt":"a very common, slightly edgy way to say"},{"t":164.1,"txt":"ruin or make a mistake. It is stronger"},{"t":167,"txt":"than mess up, but not considered a curse"},{"t":169.1,"txt":"word in most casual settings. Use this"},{"t":171.8,"txt":"when you are worried about destroying a"},{"t":173.4,"txt":"good opportunity."},{"t":175.6,"txt":"I really like this job. I hope I don't"},{"t":177.6,"txt":"screw it up. It expresses anxiety about"},{"t":180.4,"txt":"making a mistake that ruins a situation."},{"t":184.6,"txt":"something like that on my birthday,"},{"t":186,"txt":"you'd be staring at the business end of"},{"t":187.4,"txt":"a hissy fit."},{"t":189.6,"txt":">> Business end of a hissyfitit."},{"t":192.2,"txt":"This is a brilliant, complex idiom. A"},{"t":194.7,"txt":"hissy fit is a childish outburst of"},{"t":196.8,"txt":"anger. The business end usually refers"},{"t":199.5,"txt":"to the dangerous part of a tool or gun."},{"t":202.2,"txt":"Joey combines them to say you would be"},{"t":203.9,"txt":"the direct target of a massive explosive"},{"t":206.1,"txt":"tantrum."},{"t":207.9,"txt":"I forgot our anniversary and found"},{"t":209.6,"txt":"myself staring at the business end of a"},{"t":211.3,"txt":"hissy fit. It humorously describes"},{"t":214.1,"txt":"facing someone's intense and sudden"},{"t":215.7,"txt":"anger."},{"t":217.4,"txt":"Don't touch that chainsaw. That's the"},{"t":219.1,"txt":"business end. It literally warns someone"},{"t":221.9,"txt":"about the dangerous part of a tool."},{"t":229.9,"txt":">> Your sister stood me up the other night."},{"t":232.2,"txt":">> Oh, no. Don't you hate it when people"},{"t":234.6,"txt":"aren't there for you? [laughter]"},{"t":237.6,"txt":">> Well, did you try calling her?"},{"t":239.2,"txt":">> I've been trying for 2 days. When I"},{"t":241.3,"txt":"called the restaurant, they said she was"},{"t":242.6,"txt":"too busy to talk. I can't believe she's"},{"t":245,"txt":"blowing me off."},{"t":251.4,"txt":">> Your sister stood me up the other night."},{"t":254.1,"txt":">> Stood me up?"},{"t":256.2,"txt":"To stand someone up means to fail to"},{"t":258.8,"txt":"show up for a date or meeting without"},{"t":261,"txt":"cancelling. It implies disrespect and"},{"t":264,"txt":"leaving the other person waiting. It is"},{"t":266.4,"txt":"one of the most useful idioms for"},{"t":268.6,"txt":"describing dating disasters."},{"t":271.8,"txt":"I waited at the restaurant for an hour,"},{"t":273.9,"txt":"but he stood me up. It describes the"},{"t":277.2,"txt":"experience of waiting for someone who"},{"t":279.4,"txt":"never arrives."},{"t":282.5,"txt":">> She was too busy to talk."},{"t":284.2,"txt":">> I can't believe she's blowing me off."},{"t":286.9,"txt":"[music]"},{"t":287.7,"txt":">> Blowing me off."},{"t":290,"txt":"To blow someone off is slang for"},{"t":292.6,"txt":"ignoring someone. Canceling plans"},{"t":295.2,"txt":"abruptly or dismissing them as"},{"t":297.7,"txt":"unimportant. It hurts more than just"},{"t":300.3,"txt":"cancelling. It suggests the person"},{"t":302.6,"txt":"doesn't care about you at all. Try using"},{"t":305.4,"txt":"it when you feel ignored."},{"t":308.3,"txt":"I tried to talk to him about the"},{"t":310.1,"txt":"project, but he just blew me off. It"},{"t":313.4,"txt":"describes being dismissed or ignored by"},{"t":316,"txt":"someone when seeking attention."},{"t":319,"txt":"Are you blowing off our study session to"},{"t":321.3,"txt":"go to a party? It questions if someone"},{"t":324.6,"txt":"is skipping a commitment for something"},{"t":326.6,"txt":"better."},{"t":339.4,"txt":">> Dad, before I was born, did you freak"},{"t":341.8,"txt":"out at all?"},{"t":342.5,"txt":">> I'm not freaking out. I'm just saying if"},{"t":344.3,"txt":"someone had come to me with the idea of"},{"t":346.2,"txt":"this"},{"t":346.6,"txt":">> Dad. Dad, dad."},{"t":348.2,"txt":"I'm talking [clears throat] about the"},{"t":349,"txt":"whole uh baby thing. Did you uh ever get"},{"t":352.6,"txt":"this sort of panicky?"},{"t":359,"txt":">> Yeah. Before I was born, did you freak"},{"t":361.4,"txt":"out at all?"},{"t":362,"txt":">> I'm not freaking out."},{"t":363.1,"txt":">> Freak out."},{"t":364.9,"txt":"Freak out is one of the most common"},{"t":366.7,"txt":"American phrasal verbs. It means to"},{"t":369,"txt":"panic, lose control, or become extremely"},{"t":371.4,"txt":"emotional. You can freak out from fear,"},{"t":373.7,"txt":"anger, or even excitement. It's"},{"t":375.9,"txt":"essential for sounding natural in"},{"t":377.3,"txt":"English."},{"t":379,"txt":"I saw a spider on my pillow and I"},{"t":380.8,"txt":"totally freaked out. It describes a"},{"t":383.4,"txt":"sudden intense reaction of fear or"},{"t":384.9,"txt":"panic."},{"t":387.3,"txt":">> I'm just saying if someone had come to"},{"t":389.4,"txt":"me with the idea of this"},{"t":390.6,"txt":">> dad"},{"t":391.4,"txt":">> come to me with to come to someone with"},{"t":394.4,"txt":"something means to approach them to"},{"t":396.1,"txt":"present an idea, a problem or a"},{"t":397.8,"txt":"proposal. It implies a formal or serious"},{"t":400.5,"txt":"interaction where you are seeking"},{"t":401.8,"txt":"approval or a solution. Useful for"},{"t":404.2,"txt":"business contexts."},{"t":406.6,"txt":"Don't come to me with problems. Come to"},{"t":408.3,"txt":"me with solutions."},{"t":410.2,"txt":"It instructs someone on how to approach"},{"t":411.9,"txt":"a manager or leader."},{"t":418.2,"txt":"And under the bridge, I was talking"},{"t":419.5,"txt":"crazy that night. I was so drunk."},{"t":422.5,"txt":"[laughter]"},{"t":423.8,"txt":">> You don't drink?"},{"t":425.5,"txt":">> That's [clears throat] right. I don't."},{"t":428.1,"txt":"But I was I was drunk on you."},{"t":432.2,"txt":">> But okay. Yeah. So, it's not going to"},{"t":433.5,"txt":"work."},{"t":437.4,"txt":">> I said under the bridge. I was talking"},{"t":439,"txt":"crazy that night. I was so drunk."},{"t":442.4,"txt":"Talking crazy."},{"t":444.6,"txt":"Talking crazy means saying things that"},{"t":446.2,"txt":"make no sense, are unrealistic, or are"},{"t":448.6,"txt":"purely emotional. It's a great phrase to"},{"t":450.8,"txt":"use when you want to take back something"},{"t":452.2,"txt":"you said earlier, admitting that you"},{"t":454,"txt":"weren't thinking clearly."},{"t":456.5,"txt":"Ignore him. He's just tired and talking"},{"t":458.1,"txt":"crazy. It dismisses someone's speech as"},{"t":461,"txt":"nonsense due to fatigue."},{"t":465.6,"txt":">> But I was I was drunk on you."},{"t":468.6,"txt":">> Drunk on you. This is a beautiful poetic"},{"t":471.8,"txt":"metaphor. Joey isn't talking about"},{"t":474,"txt":"alcohol. He means he was so intoxicated"},{"t":476.6,"txt":"by his love and attraction to her that"},{"t":478.2,"txt":"he couldn't think straight. You can be"},{"t":480.2,"txt":"drunk on power or drunk on love."},{"t":483.8,"txt":"He was drunk on power and started firing"},{"t":486.1,"txt":"everyone. It describes someone acting"},{"t":488.6,"txt":"irrationally because of too much"},{"t":490.2,"txt":"authority."},{"t":495.9,"txt":">> So, you feel like a dad yet?"},{"t":499.4,"txt":">> No. Why?"},{"t":501.4,"txt":">> Hey, come on. You came through. You did"},{"t":503.4,"txt":"what you had to do. That's very bad."},{"t":507.4,"txt":">> Look, he's waking up."},{"t":509.1,"txt":">> Bella, how you doing?"},{"t":514.6,"txt":">> Why?"},{"t":515.9,"txt":">> Hey, come on. and you came through. You"},{"t":517.8,"txt":"did what you had to do. That's very"},{"t":520.5,"txt":">> came through."},{"t":522.4,"txt":"To come through means to succeed in a"},{"t":525,"txt":"difficult situation or to deliver on a"},{"t":527.8,"txt":"promise when it matters most. It's a"},{"t":530.7,"txt":"phrase of high praise. Use it when"},{"t":533.3,"txt":"someone saves the day or finishes a"},{"t":535.9,"txt":"tough job just in time."},{"t":539.2,"txt":"We were almost out of money, but the"},{"t":541.5,"txt":"investors came through at the last"},{"t":543.4,"txt":"minute."},{"t":544.8,"txt":"It shows how help arrived exactly when"},{"t":547.3,"txt":"it was needed."},{"t":550.2,"txt":">> Had to do as very dad. Look at"},{"t":554.4,"txt":">> very dad."},{"t":556.5,"txt":"This is a fantastic example of advanced"},{"t":559.7,"txt":"conversational English turning a noun"},{"t":562.6,"txt":"into an adjective by saying that is very"},{"t":566,"txt":"dad. Joey means the action was typical"},{"t":568.7,"txt":"of a father. You can do this with other"},{"t":571.4,"txt":"roles, too, like saying that is so very"},{"t":574.3,"txt":"New York."},{"t":576.3,"txt":"Checking the